From: Usty <usty@uase.tech>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 15:39:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] debug: temporary diagnostic panel for the assign-button
 mystery

Reviewed this code three separate times now and it's structurally
correct - the assign button and status display use the exact same
effectiveStatus variable, gated the same way, and this section has
existed since very early in the project's history. With Vercel
confirmed up to date and the code confirmed correct, guessing at more
speculative fixes isn't productive anymore.

Added a clearly-labeled, temporary yellow debug panel showing the
exact raw values driving this decision - detailData?.link?.status,
showDetail?.status, the computed effectiveStatus, the literal
comparison result, and the cars array/count - directly in the modal.
This will show us definitively what's actually happening at runtime
on the real device instead of continuing to speculate from code
review alone. Remove once diagnosed.
---
 app/dashboard/dealer/partners/page.tsx | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/app/dashboard/dealer/partners/page.tsx b/app/dashboard/dealer/partners/page.tsx
index d0cc68b..1c93f3f 100644
--- a/app/dashboard/dealer/partners/page.tsx
+++ b/app/dashboard/dealer/partners/page.tsx
@@ -358,6 +358,17 @@ export default function PartnersPage() {
                 </div>
               ) : detailData ? (
                 <>
+                  {/* TEMPORARY DEBUG - remove once we've diagnosed the assign-button issue */}
+                  <div style={{background:"#FEF3C7",border:"2px solid #F59E0B",borderRadius:"8px",padding:"0.75rem",fontSize:"0.72rem",fontFamily:"monospace",color:"#78350F"}}>
+                    <div style={{fontWeight:700,marginBottom:"0.3rem"}}>DEBUG (screenshot this and send back):</div>
+                    <div>detailData?.link?.status = {JSON.stringify(detailData?.link?.status)}</div>
+                    <div>showDetail?.status = {JSON.stringify(showDetail?.status)}</div>
+                    <div>effectiveStatus = {JSON.stringify(effectiveStatus)}</div>
+                    <div>effectiveStatus === "approved" → {String(effectiveStatus === "approved")}</div>
+                    <div>detailData?.cars = {JSON.stringify(detailData?.cars)}</div>
+                    <div>detailData?.totalCars = {JSON.stringify(detailData?.totalCars)}</div>
+                  </div>
+
                   {/* Partner info */}
                   <div style={{background:"#FAFAFA",borderRadius:"10px",padding:"1rem",display:"grid",gridTemplateColumns:"repeat(auto-fill,minmax(180px,1fr))",gap:"0.625rem"}}>
                     {[
